 the static time $ct = a + r_* - \\ell\\arctan(a/\\ell)$, with the tortoise radius $r_* = (\\ell/4)\\ln|(r - \\ell)/(r + \\ell)| + (\\ell/2)\\arctan(r/\\ell)$ at $r = a$.","caption":["The plane of $t$ and $r$ ($\\chi = 1/2$, $\\theta = \\pi/2$, $\\phi = 0$) on one side of the wall, drawn for a wall with no matter beside its tension, in a flat space, past a black hole of horizon $r_h = \\ell$. The edges of the cones are $dr/d(ct) = \\pm(r^2/\\ell^2 - \\mu/r^2)$, so $ct \\mp r_*$ is constant along a ray. The wall moves out along $r = a(t)$, and beyond it lies the mirror image of this side.","The wall comes out of the horizon as $t \\to -\\infty$ and moves out ever faster in the static time, since its expansion in its own time, $a^2 = 2\\ell c\\tau$, is that of a universe of radiation. Inside $r_h$ the static time is a direction of space, and the future there is toward smaller $r$."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains"],"version":"413b522feebb9616"}}],"gaussian_normal":[{"id":"tw","label":"$t$ and $w$","plane":["t","w"],"families":["ingoing","outgoing"],"xlabel":"$w/\\ell$","ylabel":"$ct/\\ell$","ticks":{"x":[{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"},{"at":0.5,"label":"$0.5$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$1$"},{"at":1.5,"label":"$1.5$"},{"at":2.0,"label":"$2$"}],"y":[{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"},{"at":0.5,"label":"$0.5$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$1$"},{"at":1.5,"label":"$1.5$"},{"at":2.0,"label":"$2$"}]},"box":[0,2,0,2],"to_display":[[0.0,1.0],[1.0,0.0]],"mirror":false,"rays":{"P":[[[0.0186,0.0097],[0.0173,0.0145],[0.0114,0.0225],[-0.0202,0.0545]],[[0.0522,0.0307],[0.0507,0.038],[0.0477,0.0449],[0.0366,0.0615],[0.015,0.0857],[-0.0204,0.121]],[[0.083,0.0502],[0.0811,0.0625],[0.0767,0.0742],[0.0695,0.0873],[0.0596,0.1017],[0.0454,0.1192],[0.0271,0.1397],[-0.0204,0.1877]],[[0.1114,0.071],[0.109,0.0883],[0.1032,0.1048],[0.0941,0.1226],[0.0804,0.1435],[0.062,0.1672],[0.039,0.1936],[0.0115,0.2227],[-0.0204,0.2543]],[[0.1377,0.0934],