,0.2],[0.2219,0.1813],[0.2219,0.175],[0.125,0.0781],[0.1188,0.0781],[0.1,0.0594],[0.0938,0.0594],[0.075,0.0406],[0.0688,0.0406],[0.0625,0.0344],[0.0562,0.0344],[0.0438,0.0219],[0.0375,0.0219],[0.0312,0.0156],[0.025,0.0156],[0.0188,0.0094],[0.0125,0.0094],[0.0062,0.0031],[0.0,0.0031],[0.0,0.0]]],"settings":"$\\ell = 1$, $\\mu = 1$, $k = 0$, $\\chi = \\frac{1}{2}$, $\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$, $\\phi = 0$","input":"A wall with no matter beside its tension, $\\rho = 0$, a flat space on it, $k = 0$, and a black hole of $\\mu = \\ell^2$, so that $r_h = \\ell$. It moves as $(da/d(c\\tau))^2 = \\mu/a^2$, so $a^2 = 2\\ell c\\tau$, and at the static time $ct = a + r_* - \\ell\\arctan(a/\\ell)$, with the tortoise radius $r_* = (\\ell/4)\\ln|(r - \\ell)/(r + \\ell)| + (\\ell/2)\\arctan(r/\\ell)$ at $r = a$.","caption":["The plane of $t$ and $w$ ($\\chi = 1/2$, $\\theta = \\pi/2$, $\\phi = 0$) on one side of the wall, which stands at $w = 0$, drawn for the same wall as the static chart, where $Q = 1$ and $A^2 = a^2\\left(e^{-2w/\\ell} + \\ell^2\\sinh^2(w/\\ell)/4c^2t^2\\right)$. The time $t$ is the proper time on the wall, and the cones there are those of Minkowski space.","Away from the wall the lapse $N$ falls, and the cones close onto the curve $N = 0$, $w = (\\ell/2)\\ln(1 + 4ct/\\ell)$, where the normals to the wall from neighbouring moments meet. Beyond it the coordinates go on with their time reversed, and the hatching marks that region."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains"],"version":"1f5376d30e33ba61"}}]}}
